# WIRING_REGISTER.md IS GENERATED, AND GIT MUST NOT TRY TO MERGE IT.
#
# `-merge` makes git treat the file as unmergeable: two branches that both
# changed it produce a CONFLICT rather than a textual merge.
#
# WHY THAT IS THE BEHAVIOUR WE WANT. This file has been silently mis-merged
# three times in two days, always the same way — git found two adjacent blocks
# it could interleave, kept both sides, and produced a file that looked
# plausible and was wrong. The worst of them left `table:leads` present twice
# with contradictory scores, one copy still quoting a "respond within 24 hours"
# promise the code had already stopped making. A register that asserts a fixed
# defect is still live is worse than no register.
#
# For a generated file there is nothing to merge: everything in it comes from
# the code plus scripts/wiring/annotations.mjs. The correct resolution is always
#
#     node scripts/wiring/build.mjs
#
# and a conflict is what makes somebody run it. A textual merge is what stopped
# them having to — and `Wiring register` in CI then caught it only after the
# merge had already landed on main, twice.
#
# This is the same class as the locale-JSON rule in CLAUDE.md ("resolving a
# locale conflict is not concatenation"), which came out of two production
# outages with the same cause. Here the fix can be structural, because unlike
# en.json this file has a generator.
WIRING_REGISTER.md -merge linguist-generated=true
